From 17535a89dd41b2352668963af70d960bd66579ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Johnson <neil.johnson71@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:48:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/26] ascheck: correct the generated area symbol names in the
 bndry test

ascheck/bndry/b_areas_[123].asm reference three linker generated
symbols per module:

	.word	b_Area_2_1	; 00 02
	.word	s_Area_2
	.word	l_Area_2

Only the third is a name ASLink produces.  lnkarea() and lnksect()
in lkarea.c generate exactly four forms, and the manual lists the
same four (asmlnk.txt, "Linker Generated Symbols"):

	a_<area>	the starting address of the area
	l_<area>	the length of the area
	m_<area>_n	the boundary modulus of area segment n
	s_<area>_n	the starting address of area segment n

so b_Area_2_n and s_Area_2 resolve to nothing and the link fails:

    ?ASlink-Warning-Undefined Global b_Area_2_1 referenced by
                    module b_areas_1
    ?ASlink-Warning-Undefined Global s_Area_2 referenced by
                    module b_areas_1

aslink exits 2 and the three .rst files the test exists to check
are never produced, so b_areas.bat has been unable to complete.
The names look like an older convention that the sources were never
moved off;  they appear nowhere else in the tree or the
documentation.

Which name each was meant to be is not a guess - the sources record
the values they expect:

- b_Area_2_n carries ';  00 02' in module 1 and ';  00 48' in
  modules 2 and 3, is indexed per module, and sits in a file whose
  subject is .bndry.  0x48 is 72, the least common multiple of the
  2, 3, 4, 6, 8 and 9 the modules request.  That is the boundary
  modulus of an area segment, m_<area>_n.
- s_Area_2 is not indexed, is identical in all three modules, and
  is paired with l_Area_2.  The partner of an area's length is the
  area's start, a_<area>.

Renaming them accordingly makes the link succeed and makes the
tools produce the values the sources predicted:

    0018 00 02   82  .word  m_Area_2_1  ; 00 02
    001A 00 00   83  .word  a_Area_2
    001C 00 C2   84  .word  l_Area_2
    0070 00 48   88  .word  m_Area_2_2  ; 00 48

and asxscn, which compares those columns against those comments
independently, reports 0 code differences in all three modules.

Verified:
- aslink exits 0, where it exited 2 before.
- asxscn -i on b_areas_1.rst, b_areas_2.rst and b_areas_3.rst each
  report "0 code difference(s) found", exit 0.

Also adds the two cases this unblocks to the astest corpus, taking
it from five to seven:

- bndry, which pins .even/.odd/.bndry alignment surviving
  relocation and -a base placement.
- equtst, which pins the 17 errors equtst.asm provokes on purpose,
  each annotated in the source with the code it should produce.
  Its listing is golded rather than its map:  the map holds the two
  deliberate undefined-symbol warnings, and symdef() walks the
  symbol hash table in bucket order, so their order depends on
  NCPS, NHASH and the hash function.  The listing is in source
  order and is stable.  Line 294 of that golden is the '. = 4'
  error that segmentation faulted every assembler until the
  equate() fix, so this case is what keeps it fixed.

make check now runs seven cases and passes.

